  "scope": "Actual CPU-owned 64 TX plus 64 RX ring construction/readback with conservative 256-byte prefetch tails. Linux's minimum ring policy is64; RP1 config does not set BD_RD_PREFETCH, so the tail is conservative padding using its DCFG10 formula, not claimed Linux RP1 behavior. No queue MMIO or DMA activation. Apple interfaces document the required future live mapping/cache provider; they are not implemented or replaced by this core.",
